      "writtenOn": "2022-01-06T13:41:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not going to work. This method is creating one NRI, and each NRI has a list of network requests that code for the requested network in priority order. All capabilities from the NRs inside a given NRI *must* have the same list of UIDs.\n\nSo before your change, as the comment in l.10175 explains, this was matching the entire range of UIDs for that user, and would have one layer for the enterprise capabilities and one for the default network.\n\nWith your new code, if the client passes a list of 3 ProfileNetworkPreference objects, you\u0027ll have 6 layers, with layers 2 4 and 6 being identical, and layers 3~6 never ever used because layer 2 will always match the default network of the device.\n\nBecause eventually each ProfileNetworkPreference will apply to a different set of UID ranges, what you\u0027ll need is not one NRI with a stack of requests each matching a different set. You\u0027ll need one NRI for each distinct set of UID ranges, and each NRI will have one (if no fallback) or two (if fallback) NetworkRequest objects.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10187,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 10187,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "5fd680eb0b885fc2b562e9d6f560403ba22ce494",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
